            <div xml:id="d794">

                <pb facs="0755" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-21T13:00:00-04:00">June 21, 1941—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. Your 332, June 20, 11 p.m. The British Embassy in Washington has referred
                    your suggestions to London and now informs the Department that the British
                    Government agrees to your proposal to communicate informally to Conty only
                    paragraphs 1 and 2 and perhaps the substance of subheadings 1, 2, 5 and 6 under
                    paragraph 3 of the terms quoted in the Department’s 104, June 18 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">19</hi>] 11 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">7 p.m.</hi>],
                    and to communicate the remainder of the provisions to Conty as soon as the
                    French authorities definitely express a wish to discuss terms.</p>
                <p>The British Government states that it has no doubt that you will bear in mind
                    that the British terms, as stated in the Department’s 104, were based on an
                    immediate cessation of hostilities.</p>
                <p>The British Government is keeping British headquarters in Cairo fully informed,
                    as well as General Wilson in Palestine.</p>
                <p>Can you communicate directly with Palestine or Cairo?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
